From e58dd9c2a3d6a26d3a88575858f38c13d75e0c61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 09:49:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [Channel Planning] Changes to support channel planning with
 DCS triggers

Program the driver ACS block list (= all radio channels minus the
controller-preferred set) so a driver-side DCS / autonomous channel
switch stays confined to the preferred channels, for both the Active-ACS
and CBS approaches, plus a CBS periodic-trigger save/flush/restore work-around.
Also propagates the channel-selection config knobs from beerocks_agent.conf
into the fronthaul (ap_manager/BWL HAL) process, which runs with its own
AgentDB instance and therefore could never observe them.

Key design points:

- Add a dedicated VS message SET_ACS_BLOCK_LIST (block-list only, no
  "ACS invoke 0") carrying a flat channel list; the radio is identified
  via the beerocks action-header radio_mac().
- The CBS periodic save/flush/trigger/restore is orchestrated in the
  ap_manager TRIGGER_CBS handler (backend-agnostic), not in HAL.
  Restore uses an Agent-side per-radio cache of the last-programmed
  block list (not a driver read-back); acs_get_block_chan_list() is
  only a presence check.
- CBS also programs the block list on Channel Selection Request (in addition
  to its rank-first CSA). Block-list semantics respect EasyMesh standards:
  |P| == 1 -> flush only; |P| > 1 -> flush + block all non-preferred channels.
- Active-ACS behaviour is unchanged (internal refactor only).

Config gating (strict, per-knob):

- enable_auto_chansel_handling is the PRIMARY gate. When disabled, none of the
  proprietary functionality runs (no pre-selection rules, no block list, no CBS,
  no Active-ACS) and the flow is byte-for-byte the legacy cumulative-preference
  selection - preserving the Test-Harness / Data-Validation "fallback only"
  behaviour.
- The block-list mechanism, pre-selection rules, CBS rank-first selection and
  Active-ACS are additionally guarded by their specific knob
  (cbs_based_chansel_enable / active_acs_chansel_enable). With
  enable_auto_chansel_handling=1 but both approach knobs disabled, no block list
  is programmed and only the cumulative-preference fallback runs.
- The two approaches are mutually exclusive. If both cbs_based_chansel_enable and
  active_acs_chansel_enable are enabled (with the primary gate on), the code logs
  a warning and falls back to cumulative-preference channel selection.
- cbs_trigger_periodic_interval is an INDEPENDENT knob: if non-zero, the periodic
  CBS trigger runs on that period regardless of the three flags above (supports
  proprietary channel-selection apps that consume the CBS cache with
  enable_auto_chansel_handling=0). When the CBS approach is enabled but the
  interval was left at 0, it is overridden to a default (3600s), logged once.

TLVF (YAML sources only; AutoGenerated is produced by codegen):

- beerocks_message_action.yaml: add ACTION_BACKHAUL_HOSTAP_SET_ACS_BLOCK_LIST (92)
  and ACTION_APMANAGER_HOSTAP_SET_ACS_BLOCK_LIST (94), bump enum ends.
- beerocks_message_backhaul.yaml / beerocks_message_apmanager.yaml: add the
  SET_ACS_BLOCK_LIST classes with block_channels_size + block_channels list.
- beerocks_message_apmanager.yaml: extend cACTION_APMANAGER_CONFIGURE with
  cbs_based_chansel_enable and active_acs_chansel_enable (uint8_t/bool), carried
  alongside the existing certification_mode / multi_ap_profile / local_gw /
  radio_disable fields.

BWL HAL (ap_wlan_hal_nl80211):

- ap_wlan_hal.h: add acs_clear_block_chan_list(), acs_set_block_chan_list(),
  acs_get_block_chan_list() pure-virtuals.
- nl80211: refactor start_platform_acs() steps (2)/(3) onto the new primitives;
  implement the primitives over the base radio wpa_ctrl socket
  ("ACS clear_block_chan_list" / "ACS set_block_chan_list" / "ACS get_block_chan_list").
- process_nl80211_event: explicitly handle the non-AWGN DCS interference types
  (WLAN, CW, OBSS) with an informational log stating the switch is left to the
  driver's autonomous DCS (constrained by the block list / CBS cache); AWGN path
  is unchanged.
- process_nl80211_event: allow the radio-scoped channel-switch events
  (CSA_Finished, CSA_Started, CTRL_Channel_Switch, ACS_Completed,
  DFS_RADAR_Detected) to bypass the per-VAP vap_id resolution guard. On MLD radios
  these events arrive with the base/link iface name (wlan1 / wlan1_link0 / wlan1_1)
  which the per-VAP resolution can fail to map; without this they were dropped and
  a driver-initiated (DCS) channel switch never reached the Agent, so the mandatory
  Operating Channel Report was not generated. The CSA handlers are radio-scoped and
  do not index available_vaps[vap_id], so a radio-level sentinel is safe.
- whm: implement acs_set/clear over WiFi.Radio.{i}.ACS.BlockChanList and trigger_cbs
  over WiFi.Radio.{i}.CBS.Enable=1; acs_get_block_chan_list() is a deliberate stub
  (pending pWHM data-model confirmation) - non-blocking because restore uses the
  Agent-side cache.
- dummy/dwpald/onewifi: inert stubs returning false.
- No functional change to the existing HAL gates: refresh_radio_info()'s rank
  baseline (cbs_based_chansel_enable ? 0 : 1) and read_acs_report()'s early return
  remain as-is; they simply now see the real conf value.

Agent:

- son_slave_thread: relay ACTION_BACKHAUL_HOSTAP_SET_ACS_BLOCK_LIST to the ap_manager
  as ACTION_APMANAGER_HOSTAP_SET_ACS_BLOCK_LIST.
- son_slave_thread: populate the two new CONFIGURE fields from AgentDB::device_conf
  (values already validated / mutually-exclusive-checked in beerocks_agent_main.cpp).
- ap_manager: add SET_ACS_BLOCK_LIST handler (clear + set, cache the programmed list);
  wrap TRIGGER_CBS to flush the cached block list before "CBS enable 1" and restore it
  afterwards; also populate the cache from the Active-ACS PLATFORM_ACS exclude channels.
- ap_manager: cache cbs_based_chansel_enable / active_acs_chansel_enable from CONFIGURE
  and use them in create_ap_wlan_hal() instead of reading AgentDB (not populated in the
  fronthaul process, so hal_conf.*_chansel_enable was always false there).
- ChannelSelectionTask: add apply_preferred_channel_block_list(); the CBS branch
  programs the block list (invoke_acs=false); Active-ACS keeps using
  send_acs_list_to_platform().
- ChannelSelectionTask: resolve_usable_bandwidth() converts generic bandwidth
  mappings to the channel-specific/usable variant per band from the driver
  supported_bw_list; applied to Rule 1 and as a universal safety net in
  send_channel_switch_request() to avoid "No valid PHY mode found" failures.
- ChannelSelectionTask: normalize the preferred channel set to beacon-channel
  numbered op-classes so a single-channel preference is not inflated into a
  multi-channel block list.
- ChannelSelectionTask: driver-initiated CSA is reported via the existing
  CSA-notification -> unsolicited Operating Channel Report path (mandatory OCR for
  every channel switch); no re-selection is run for a driver-autonomous DCS switch.
- ChannelSelectionTask: diagnostic-only WARNING in handle_vs_channels_list_response()
  when every (chan,bw) entry carries the same positive rank (fingerprint of the
  non-CBS baseline rather than a driver "ACS show_report"). No control-flow change.

Note: whm acs_get_block_chan_list() is intentionally left as a stub pending
      pWHM read-back-param confirmation.

Signed-off-by: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
